    {
      "slug": "office-fridge-lunch-thief",
      "script": "Who stole my lunch? For three weeks straight, someone ate it from the office fridge. HR shrugged; my manager shrugged. I bought an identical container, wrote HR SAMPLE, DO NOT EAT, UNDER REVIEW in bold red marker, packed my actual leftovers extra spicy, and left it at nine. By eleven, one accounting intern sprinted toward the break room, pale and asking whether sample meant a drug test. She had eaten half before checking the label twice. I said nothing. That afternoon, she confessed to HR and admitted the thefts went back to January, all to explain why she was hungry. The office fridge has had a padlock ever since—and it is not mine. Would you trust that fridge?",
      "editor_note": "Rewritten to 118 words with a short question hook, all protected numbers and entities preserved, and a specific closing question."
    },
    {
      "slug": "car-dealership-hidden-fee-recording",
      "script": "Mandatory—or pure profit? The finance manager called the eight hundred dollar dealer prep fee non-negotiable and required by the manufacturer. I agreed, without mentioning I had recorded the negotiation on my phone, which is legal in my state. Two days later, I found the exact same fee waived for a friend at the same dealership that same week and called to cancel. The manager insisted it was mandatory for every customer, no exceptions. I drove back and asked for the general manager directly. Then I played eleven seconds: his finance guy calling the fee basically just extra profit, don't worry about it. The general manager's face changed. He refunded the full eight hundred dollars on the spot, comped an oil change package, and the finance manager was gone from the floor within a week. Would you have played the tape?",
      "editor_note": "Rewritten to 140 words with a short question hook, all protected numbers and entities preserved, and a specific closing question."
    },
